### WorldCover products
Two versions of the WorldCover products are available:
- WorldCover 2020 produced using v100 of the algorithm
- WorldCover 2021 produced using v200 of the algorithm
Since the WorldCover maps for 2020 and 2021 were generated with different algorithm versions (v100 and v200, respectively), changes between the maps include both changes in real land cover and changes due to the used algorithms.

### WorldCover Annual Composites
Since June 2023 you can also access the WorldCover annual composites, a set of yearly median and percentiles composites at 10m resolution, derived from the Copernicus Sentinel-1 and Sentinel-2 archives, for the years 2020 and 2021.
The products can be visualized and explored using the [WorldCover viewer](https://viewer.esa-worldcover.org/worldcover). WMS layers are also available from the [Terrascope](https://terrascope.be/en) WMS service.
- WMTS: [https://services.terrascope.be/wmts/v2](https://services.terrascope.be/wmts/v2)
- WMS: [https://services.terrascope.be/wms/v2https://services.terrascope.be/wms/v2](https://services.terrascope.be/wms/v2)
- GAMMA0 layers: WORLDCOVER_2020_S1_VVVHratio, WORLDCOVER_2021_S1_VVVHratio
- RGB layers: WORLDCOVER_2020_S2_TCC, WORLDCOVER_2021_S2_TCC
- FALSE COLOR layers: WORLDCOVER_2020_S2_FCC, WORLDCOVER_2021_S2_FCC
- NDVI layers: WORLDCOVER_2020_S2_NDVI, WORLDCOVER_2021_S2_NDVI 
- SWIR layers: WORLDCOVER_2020_S2_SWIR, WORLDCOVER_2021_S2_SWIR 
[https://services.terrascope.be/wmts/v2](https://services.terrascope.be/wmts/v2)
[https://services.terrascope.be/wms/v2https://services.terrascope.be/wms/v2](https://services.terrascope.be/wms/v2)
The products are available free of charge for all users on [Terrascope](https://terrascope.be/en)and the [AWS Open Data Registry](https://registry.opendata.aws/esa-worldcover-vito/%22%20HYPERLINK%20%22https://registry.opendata.aws/esa-worldcover-vito-composites/). The Sentinel-1 and Sentinel-2 composites are accessible on the public AWS buckets (eu-central-1 region) s3://esa-worldcover-s1 and s3://esa-worldcover-s2 respectively.  A grid of the products is provided [here](https://esa-worldcover.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/esa_worldcover_grid_composites.fgb). This FlatGeobuf file can be opened remotely in QGIS or python and can be used to retrieve the S3 paths (or URL links) of the desired tiles.
Each product is delivered as a series of Cloud-Optimized GeoTIFFs (COGs) in WSG84 projection in a grid of 1 by 1 degrees and at approximately 10m resolution, except for the SWIR composite which is provided at 20m resolution. (Actual resolution in degrees is provided in the metadata table). The Sentinel-2 composites were produced from the L2A archive. The GAMMA0 composite was produced by pre-processing the Sentinel-1 GRD products using [GAMMA software](https://www.gamma-rs.ch/). More information about the products generation and pre-processing steps is available in the WorldCover V200 [Product User Manual](https://esa-worldcover.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/v200/2021/docs/WorldCover_PUM_V2.0.pdf).
